{"id": "EUVD-2026-91445", "enisaUuid": "aee9b6ec-4c72-37dc-afaf-d6fad6888615", "description": "Zebra zebrad 4.4.0 and zebra-script 6.0.0 fail to enforce a ZIP-244 consensus rule, accepting V5 transparent inputs signed with SIGHASH_SINGLE that lack a corresponding output. Attackers can broadcast crafted V5 transactions with more inputs than outputs that Zebra accepts but zcashd rejects, causing a network consensus split.", "datePublished": "2026-10-02T11:38:12", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-02T15:16:42", "baseScore": 8.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/ZcashFoundation/zebra/security/advisories/GHSA-pvmv-cwg8-v6c8", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/zebra-4.4.0-consensus-divergence-via-v5-sighash-single-without-output"], "aliases": ["GHSA-gm38-j348-x4mq", "CVE-2026-104435"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1ada0ce9-bdc2-386c-8fa7-cebb53e6d703", "product": {"name": "zebra", "vendor": {"name": "ZcashFoundation"}}, "product_version": "4.4.0 <4.4.1"}, {"id": "1fd9cc6d-b566-37c5-8159-d683c862e0be", "product": {"name": "zebra", "vendor": {"name": "ZcashFoundation"}}, "product_version": "6.0.0 <6.0.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "c52e219c-64c6-3bb6-8ae7-6765c2d7254e", "vendor": {"name": "ZcashFoundation"}}], "isExploited": false}